// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5957 new: Browser Extension Force Install via Policy Detection (Windows, macOS, Linux)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5957
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Suspicious Browser Extension Force Install via Policy on Windows
// Sigma ID: 6f14defd-2f56-441f-907c-957731b58aa2
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001, defense-evasion, T1112
// Description: Detects the creation of browser extension force-install policy entries in the Windows registry.
//   The ExtensionInstallForcelist policy silently installs extensions that users cannot disable or
//   remove. ExtensionSettings allows configuring force-installed extensions with auto-granted
//   permissions. Adversaries may abuse these to persist malicious browser extensions across reboots
//   without user interaction.
// False positives:
//   - Enterprise IT administrators deploying browser extensions via Group Policy
//   - MDM tools managing browser extensions in corporate environments
// References:
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionInstallForcelist
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionSettings
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-policies#extensioninstallforcelist
//   - https://support.google.com/chrome/a/answer/9037717
//   - https://github.com/praetorian-inc/ChromeAlone
//   - https://blog.google/threat-analysis-group/isp-level-threat-actors/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/526405083b950916d7e784ee66c6fab0b0211c44/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_win_browser_extension_force_install_policy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 3 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Policies\\Google\\Chrome\\ExtensionInstallForcelist.*$" or RegistryKey contains "\\Policies\\Google\\Chrome\\ExtensionSettings") or (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\ExtensionInstallForcelist.*$" or RegistryKey contains "\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\ExtensionSettings") or (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Policies\\Chromium\\ExtensionInstallForcelist.*$" or RegistryKey contains "\\Policies\\Chromium\\ExtensionSettings")
